    SECTION 8 — FAQ
  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━{%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="dp-faq" aria-label="Frequently asked questions">
    <div class="dp-container">
      <span class="dp-eyebrow">FAQs</span>
      <div class="dp-faq__grid">
        <div class="dp-faq__item">
          <h3 class="dp-faq__q">Is this program only for hygienists?</h3>
          <p class="dp-faq__a">No — dentists, dental assistants, and dental students are all welcome. We primarily designed the program for hygienists because of the daily patient touchpoints, but any licensed dental professional can apply.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="dp-faq__item">
          <h3 class="dp-faq__q">Is there any cost to join?</h3>
          <p class="dp-faq__a">Absolutely not. Joining is free. There's no inventory to buy, no minimum sales requirement, and no ongoing fees. You receive a free product kit upon approval to experience the products yourself.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="dp-faq__item">
          <h3 class="dp-faq__q">How does the commission work with subscriptions?</h3>
          <p class="dp-faq__a">You earn 15% on a patient's first purchase and 10% on every subsequent subscription order. This means a single recommendation can generate recurring monthly income for as long as that patient subscribes.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="dp-faq__item">
          <h3 class="dp-faq__q">When and how do I get paid?</h3>
          <p class="dp-faq__a">Commissions are tracked in real time via your dashboard and paid out monthly — via direct deposit or PayPal — with a minimum payout threshold of $25.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="dp-faq__item">
          <h3 class="dp-faq__q">Can I give my patients a discount?</h3>
          <p class="dp-faq__a">Yes. Every partner receives a unique promo code that gives your patients 10% off their first order. This makes the recommendation feel like a genuine gift — not a sales pitch.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="dp-faq__item">
          <h3 class="dp-faq__q">What is nano-hydroxyapatite and is it safe?</h3>
          <p class="dp-faq__a">Nano-hydroxyapatite (n-Ha) is the naturally occurring mineral that comprises ~97% of tooth enamel. It has been clinically studied since the 1970s, is recognized by the Japanese Ministry of Health as an approved anti-cavity agent, and is considered safe for all ages including pregnant patients.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

